[{:db/id "q-104151/selection/db7b54c70af5b3285ee1472686b4ed766a980f47020d1c12bfcdfec823bd2559" :answer/id #uuid "c315d17a-8d08-5f46-a406-dbc6dbf56435" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}+{v}^{2})^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104151/selection/4a3a96af0d96f0403076396a29e5f7ce72eb1ea2570fa39ae9ef0fa6bc6ef878" :answer/id #uuid "bc35329c-cdb3-52a4-83d0-badeab013971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u+v)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104151/selection/11b59cdb36a977720d02bbf915df566ff3cafe2395801b92a444ff690feb3f89" :answer/id #uuid "72513cd1-ed0c-5758-9f86-3910518bf8b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104151/selection/5bee3f4a787cd16a75abdc372700470e40e60718d665af74d5ed2a149dc952c8" :answer/id #uuid "7b8bee01-6009-5cc9-b4da-b11c79f9139e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104151/selection/df0314b975a0ffadfcabb7d6d5ccd78b1f8f9e090847dbefb15a94db7a64b397" :answer/id #uuid "b041447f-cfcb-557f-8820-7eaa624d4c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(u-v)^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104151/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e84f03c-45f8-5453-9d86-1686a4f61bce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104151/selection/5bee3f4a787cd16a75abdc372700470e40e60718d665af74d5ed2a149dc952c8" :answer-field/choices ["q-104151/selection/db7b54c70af5b3285ee1472686b4ed766a980f47020d1c12bfcdfec823bd2559" "q-104151/selection/4a3a96af0d96f0403076396a29e5f7ce72eb1ea2570fa39ae9ef0fa6bc6ef878" "q-104151/selection/11b59cdb36a977720d02bbf915df566ff3cafe2395801b92a444ff690feb3f89" "q-104151/selection/5bee3f4a787cd16a75abdc372700470e40e60718d665af74d5ed2a149dc952c8" "q-104151/selection/df0314b975a0ffadfcabb7d6d5ccd78b1f8f9e090847dbefb15a94db7a64b397"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104151" :question/id #uuid "f8eee31e-0f84-552f-8351-0fc856c749dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-104151" :question/problem "$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(u,v)$ parametrizes the surface defined in Cartesian coordinates as \n${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{3}=0.$\n What is the third component of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $z=f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{3} & =0 \\\\ z & =\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨x,\\,y,\\,\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain the vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $r$ is $\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104151/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f686e8d-5080-529c-b581-221892921cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104151"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104179/selection/61cd9498c58beb2def50b159c54fa013966c1148a12b598418dc464cbc3b9b61" :answer/id #uuid "034a13a3-e781-5842-8bf8-06461af74f75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2-u-v}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104179/selection/147fd6d5610ccb19f3f244dafd6283d0f812b42040db46b1db3bf0db88053d89" :answer/id #uuid "12c184f9-1c9c-5efb-ae68-bd422886515d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4-u-v}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104179/selection/f63766eaba87b14e563287e9390a839227040320fd42fd0ec6ed01e704cd1b4c" :answer/id #uuid "893eca1f-0da5-54e8-9c5a-8280aab69731" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2+u-v}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104179/selection/e24b9c74e6362dcab6bc96369d2f4c9e2a9febf545bc5a173a9f91c360aac6dd" :answer/id #uuid "464c331c-2bd2-59f4-b698-2b90c86bc867" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4-u-v}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104179/selection/d2ac676d68ec6482adb9b4514a1e4ef0d918a8c3f5529b81056ad1049c69e58e" :answer/id #uuid "23100d53-d663-5266-82f4-f67d51776d1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2-u-v}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104179/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6285d276-1886-507a-a7a6-cfbc81014574" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104179/selection/e24b9c74e6362dcab6bc96369d2f4c9e2a9febf545bc5a173a9f91c360aac6dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-104179/selection/61cd9498c58beb2def50b159c54fa013966c1148a12b598418dc464cbc3b9b61" "q-104179/selection/147fd6d5610ccb19f3f244dafd6283d0f812b42040db46b1db3bf0db88053d89" "q-104179/selection/f63766eaba87b14e563287e9390a839227040320fd42fd0ec6ed01e704cd1b4c" "q-104179/selection/e24b9c74e6362dcab6bc96369d2f4c9e2a9febf545bc5a173a9f91c360aac6dd" "q-104179/selection/d2ac676d68ec6482adb9b4514a1e4ef0d918a8c3f5529b81056ad1049c69e58e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104179" :question/id #uuid "137fac61-848f-5605-9990-3509ba74c2b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-104179" :question/problem "$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $r(u,v)$ parametrizes the surface defined in Cartesian coordinates as \n$\\frac{x+y}{6}+\\frac{z-1}{2}=\\frac{1}{6}.$\n What is the third component of $r?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $z=f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{6}+\\frac{z-1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ \\frac{z-1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x+y}{6} \\\\ \\frac{z-1}{2} & =\\frac{1-x-y}{6} \\\\ z & =\\frac{4-x-y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨x,\\,y,\\,\\frac{4-x-y}{3}⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain the vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\frac{4-u-v}{3}⟩\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $r$ is $\\frac{4-u-v}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4f686e8d-5080-529c-b581-221892921cc2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104290/selection/4396e9b5b378e73f37c569a5dc88d1d38b572730f898e9f6aaa324fb2f1150b0" :answer/id #uuid "581f1dde-31e5-5675-ba28-901f6fa21f8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2r" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104290/selection/00e5a9633b225d28595eef377d7295907af8a777c6ac14b5df6d47bff03fb6fc" :answer/id #uuid "ea7900ef-3018-5ff9-878c-a6bd05b1671b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{r}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104290/selection/2b572d0b6ef46a2c9ce9765c475325a5d52d4e158fef7efeda8b51f5dc29f2f9" :answer/id #uuid "d2141598-0071-5269-b9f5-ad5acf6bad89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104290/selection/9c27af596a54023fbd5fabfca2e1b7c62866955f063ece27d016f40b14f493e8" :answer/id #uuid "881e9f53-642e-5201-bfd8-85dc24674352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{r}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104290/selection/3241760d793c1deb77d5b8fed071cd166050543adeae163ee6445a08f221d6dc" :answer/id #uuid "f57b53e4-175d-5385-9a33-73a2ae525c48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104290/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b68f42b7-96fb-5fa3-a618-dbefcae9031f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104290/selection/4396e9b5b378e73f37c569a5dc88d1d38b572730f898e9f6aaa324fb2f1150b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-104290/selection/4396e9b5b378e73f37c569a5dc88d1d38b572730f898e9f6aaa324fb2f1150b0" "q-104290/selection/00e5a9633b225d28595eef377d7295907af8a777c6ac14b5df6d47bff03fb6fc" "q-104290/selection/2b572d0b6ef46a2c9ce9765c475325a5d52d4e158fef7efeda8b51f5dc29f2f9" "q-104290/selection/9c27af596a54023fbd5fabfca2e1b7c62866955f063ece27d016f40b14f493e8" "q-104290/selection/3241760d793c1deb77d5b8fed071cd166050543adeae163ee6445a08f221d6dc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104290" :question/id #uuid "d88762f9-7faa-5003-8c13-d18404076d4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104290" :question/problem "$$\nf(r,\\theta )=⟨r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\text{_____}⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(r,\\theta )$ parametrizes the surface defined in cylindrical polar coordinates as \n$4{r}^{2}-{z}^{2}=0$\nfor $z\\ge 0.$ What is the third component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $z=f(r,\\theta ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{r}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =4{r}^{2} \\\\ z & =\\sqrt{4{r}^{2}} \\\\ z & =2r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are given that $z\\ge 0.$\n\nIf $(r,\\theta ,z)$ are the cylindrical coordinates of a point and $(x,y,z)$ are the corresponding Cartesian coordinates of that point, then we have\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z=z.\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nf=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,z⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $z=2r,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf(r,\\theta )=⟨r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,2r⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $2r.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104290/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "097a87b7-38e3-5002-b460-2edccb9ce85c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104290"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104368/selection/7fbec49c6572b959623fd6f5ef1b5828303718216a5f674236add853a5cdf6b2" :answer/id #uuid "c7567391-d9d3-51c6-9570-dcec53c18ee4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104368/selection/fc848c75983f5c9cc652a3f03bce2f9b9434d3131d45b8d3cb191bfff1c6f981" :answer/id #uuid "144b866d-f52d-5c1c-8a80-0c69d699910c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104368/selection/f0a9ee435d54bdda587baffdee6fcc34e0b9e0e418eb17c3d07fa3412833ad97" :answer/id #uuid "1047f734-e4ef-5ef8-9ff6-2f9e3712abc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104368/selection/a66b945d780502062d084c63393d09d79976256153841fa02589ad0402eb207e" :answer/id #uuid "ce5de037-707f-595f-b502-aaac90e582b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104368/selection/154a13b6908693c60e7d9d80cf9b16b745ef660d09480749bf1a3f3ccd81e330" :answer/id #uuid "862df4d6-bcbb-53c9-94e3-a7f8b7f06d8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{3}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104368/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "92c2657d-bd5d-577d-93ea-9ecb446ac1e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104368/selection/7fbec49c6572b959623fd6f5ef1b5828303718216a5f674236add853a5cdf6b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-104368/selection/7fbec49c6572b959623fd6f5ef1b5828303718216a5f674236add853a5cdf6b2" "q-104368/selection/fc848c75983f5c9cc652a3f03bce2f9b9434d3131d45b8d3cb191bfff1c6f981" "q-104368/selection/f0a9ee435d54bdda587baffdee6fcc34e0b9e0e418eb17c3d07fa3412833ad97" "q-104368/selection/a66b945d780502062d084c63393d09d79976256153841fa02589ad0402eb207e" "q-104368/selection/154a13b6908693c60e7d9d80cf9b16b745ef660d09480749bf1a3f3ccd81e330"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104368" :question/id #uuid "eaa8239e-29e5-5977-9d1a-1751cf1acc74" :question/math-academy-id "q-104368" :question/problem "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ parametrizes the surface defined in spherical polar coordinates as \n$\\rho =ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .$\nWhat is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "If $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nf=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $\\rho =ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ϕ{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $ϕ{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-104368/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e6352a6-6505-517a-9a70-7c5701eda938"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104368"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104378/selection/b37b782d8bf58c4cccf9560725f3beeeb540e434ec044b5f8259a39f46a8d4a7" :answer/id #uuid "3ade17df-2b42-5f0a-a452-b6b26266325a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104378/selection/551541bc3fc83a5ac74c10fef9c02fb5a9ce8b99fbd1f0b5d92b2ba5edb614ab" :answer/id #uuid "df350d58-c4d8-585d-b4ce-dece66b8b1df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104378/selection/fc848c75983f5c9cc652a3f03bce2f9b9434d3131d45b8d3cb191bfff1c6f981" :answer/id #uuid "2181fc1a-93b5-5a4f-b537-5e1257f2bbb4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104378/selection/1584994fa3360f5ae9586e0866bd3b2dd951f72247da4aea09ddda81a200e763" :answer/id #uuid "d5fa5fac-c7d6-5164-bc27-c14d13354f85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104378/selection/1ed3b3191730df7b8dd23b7a1e80d28bc8ae9e24233f27de901dc763aba43287" :answer/id #uuid "b3a4f705-6671-579c-a5d2-51c113a001f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104378/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dda4e1ea-8286-5816-9a57-f12f29bb748a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104378/selection/1ed3b3191730df7b8dd23b7a1e80d28bc8ae9e24233f27de901dc763aba43287" :answer-field/choices ["q-104378/selection/b37b782d8bf58c4cccf9560725f3beeeb540e434ec044b5f8259a39f46a8d4a7" "q-104378/selection/551541bc3fc83a5ac74c10fef9c02fb5a9ce8b99fbd1f0b5d92b2ba5edb614ab" "q-104378/selection/fc848c75983f5c9cc652a3f03bce2f9b9434d3131d45b8d3cb191bfff1c6f981" "q-104378/selection/1584994fa3360f5ae9586e0866bd3b2dd951f72247da4aea09ddda81a200e763" "q-104378/selection/1ed3b3191730df7b8dd23b7a1e80d28bc8ae9e24233f27de901dc763aba43287"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104378" :question/id #uuid "b3e84b4d-aff6-5599-897e-3da92a2fc9f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-104378" :question/problem "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨\\text{ _____ },\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ parametrizes the surface defined in spherical polar coordinates as \n$ϕ=\\rho \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .$\nWhat is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of the surface in the form $\\rho =f(\\theta ,ϕ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ϕ & =\\rho \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\rho  & =ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found by using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\n$$\n\nNow, a point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nf=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $\\rho =ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,ϕ\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-104378/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e6352a6-6505-517a-9a70-7c5701eda938"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104378"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
